   727	\section{Generation of a neighbor candidate state} %\section{Переход к новому решению}
   728	A process of constructing a neighbor candidate state is shown in Procedure~\ref{transit}. %Генерация нового состояния-кандидата приведена в процедуре~\ref{transit}.
   729	
   730	\SetAlgorithmName{Algorithm}{Algorithm list}{} 
   731	\SetAlgoCaptionSeparator{.} 
   732	\DontPrintSemicolon
   733	\SetKwProg{Proc}{Procedure}{}{End}
   734	\SetKw{Return}{Return}
   735	\begin{algorithm}[h]
   736		\label{transit}
   737		\caption{Constructing a neighbor candidate state}
   738		\SetKwData{z}{$z$}
   739		\SetKwData{w}{$w$}
   740		\SetKwData{numOfEdgesToFix}{$fixEdgesN$}
   741		\SetKwData{generateNeighbourCandidate}{$GenerateNeighbourCandidate$}
   742		\SetKwFunction{updateFixedEdges}{$UpdateFixedEdgesQueue$}
   743		\SetKwFunction{runBlossomAlgorithm}{$RunEdmondsAlgorithm$}
   744		\SetKwFunction{runHopcroftAlgorithm}{$RunHopcroftKarpAlgorithm$}
   745		\BlankLine
   746		
   747		\Proc{\generateNeighbourCandidate{\z, \w, \numOfEdgesToFix}}{
   748			\updateFixedEdges{\z, \w, \numOfEdgesToFix}\;
   749	
   750			\eIf{tours \z and \w are directed}{
   751				\runHopcroftAlgorithm{}\;
   752			} {
   753				\runBlossomAlgorithm{}\;
   754			}  
   755	
   756			\Return \z, \w\;
   757		}
   758	\end{algorithm}
   759	
   760	The algorithm receives as input the current state as the vertex-disjoint cycle covers $z$ and $w$, and the parameter $fixEdgesN$ that set the size of a queue of edges that are fixed in the graph $z$ and the corresponding perfect matching.

