codex
The generator now passes every local gate, including a 40,000-instance stress check of the compact invariant route and an additional no-tool ansatz attack. The remaining required evidence is external: the prescribed four-vendor hardening harness cannot score even one attempt because the configured OpenRouter key returns HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” on every redraw. I’m preserving those tool-owned error transcripts and marking the result as not yet ship-certified rather than treating API failures as oracle failures.
codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator for the paper’s complementary directed Hamiltonian-tour problem.

Key results:

- Planted certificates: 16/16 verified.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 7,408,512 successor visits across eight instances.
- Compact invariant route: verified 20/20, bounded by 192 exact operations.
- Canonical-key relabelling checks: 80/80.
- G9 answer size: 98 characters, 96 bits.

Files:

- [gen_1901_09651.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1901.09651/gen_1901_09651.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1901.09651/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1901.09651/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1901.09651/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
